& [SJS]
  + Situation: Cantor can construct and bind a model-facing packet but its shell still collapses preparation dispatch response receipt and admission into one conceptual step
  + Justification: explicit immutable phases expose where a future adapter may perform an effect and where deterministic host verification resumes
  + Solution: implement a zero-effect supplied-value lifecycle now and reserve physical provider provenance for a separately activated adapter

& [Delineation]
  + preparation validates packet self-integrity
  + fixture dispatch records only a state-machine event
  + fixture response records caller-supplied bytes and their digest
  + canonical admission reconstructs the packet and compares the supplied response to retained fixture evidence
  + none of these phases proves a real model process transport or producer

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + one enum fixes four phases and one sequence number fixes their ordering zero through three
  + optional dispatch marker response response digest and admitted flag are determined completely by phase
  + envelope and response digests use distinct domain tags over deterministic compact JSON
  + transition functions preserve the envelope and every already-recorded field byte-for-byte

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty forbids fixture state names from inflating into provider-execution claims
  + Security requires local packet validation before preparation and canonical reconstruction before admission
  + Planner fixes legal successor transitions and counters
  + Weaver joins packet dispatch marker supplied response and canonical record into one trace
  + Scribe retains the exact response digest and transition state
  + Refiner keeps effectful adapter evidence absent from the pure state machine
  + Observer validates each intermediate state plus the complete fixture run

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated dispatch_lifecycle forms pure transitions fixture-run projection normalization and adversarial tests
  + keep all provider process network stream and timing behavior under a separate future lock

& [Rollback]
  + additive module exports and tests remove without changing predecessor forms or behavior
